 plain="""An engineer sets the trainer's attention implementation to `triton` because the inference engine uses a backend of that name, hoping the two will produce matching numbers. The trainer refuses the name at once. The case trains the idea that two components using the same word do not mean the same thing: each validates settings against its own list, and the error that prints that list is the fastest documentation.""",
 check=[("✓", "The engine's backend names and the trainer's implementation names are separate lists."),
        ("✗", "Using the same kernel name on both sides makes their log probabilities match.", "Matching numbers needs a specific supported pairing (here, only on Hopper GPUs), not matching names."),
        ("✓", "An error message that lists valid values is the quickest reference.")],
